Vendored C++ robotstxtbing payload — provenance
===============================================

The files listed below are a copied, SHA-pinned snapshot of the independent
`robotstxtbing` Bing-compatibility library. They are NOT downloaded or fetched
at configure, build, test, or install time; they are vendored source. The
package builds, installs, tests, and runs without a sibling checkout or network
access.

This record is the Bing counterpart of the Google matcher provenance in
`inst/PROVENANCE` and the Yandex matcher provenance in
`inst/vendor/robotstxtyandex/PROVENANCE`. It is a separate file; the Google and
Yandex provenance and their vendored hashes are unchanged.

Manifest-only status (import boundary)
--------------------------------------
This provenance and the machine-readable manifest
(`inst/vendor/robotstxtbing/MANIFEST.dcf`) freeze the approved payload identity
and per-file hashes BEFORE any behavior is imported. No production C++ payload
is vendored into `src/` by this step; the byte-for-byte import into the vendor
root (`src/vendor/robotstxtbing/`) is performed by a later slice (BI3). The Bing
matcher therefore remains `capability_unavailable` until every activation gate
passes (BI5).

